# deploy/docker-compose.override.yml.template — host override for the Postgres and
# Redis DATA directories ONLY (remediation item 4.3; ADR-0004).
#
# NORMALLY NOT NEEDED. Since item 4.3 the base docker-compose.yml binds both data
# directories itself, fail-closed:
#     ${OPENBRAIN_DATA_DIR:-/mnt/user/appdata/open-brain}/pgdata     -> /var/lib/postgresql/data
#     ${OPENBRAIN_DATA_DIR:-/mnt/user/appdata/open-brain}/redis-data -> /data
# A host whose data lives under one parent directory with those two leaf names sets
# OPENBRAIN_DATA_DIR in .env (or uses the default) and needs NO override file.
#
# A host needs this override only when OPENBRAIN_DATA_DIR cannot express its data
# path: the two directories sit under different parents or carry other names. Then:
#   1. cp deploy/docker-compose.override.yml.template docker-compose.override.yml
#   2. Replace both /CHANGE_ME/... sources with the real absolute paths. An unedited
#      copy fails closed: Docker refuses to start a container whose bind source is
#      missing (create_host_path: false), so nothing starts on an empty directory.
#   3. Render gate before any `up` (prints volume fields only — never print or save a
#      full render, it inlines .env.secrets values):
#        docker compose config --format json \
#          | jq -c '[.services.postgres.volumes[], .services.redis.volumes[]]
#                   | map({type, source, target, chp: .bind.create_host_path})'
#      Every entry must show "type":"bind" and "chp":false, with the real sources.
#
# Rules for this file:
#   - LONG syntax only, with bind.create_host_path: false. A short-syntax entry
#     (`- /path:/var/lib/postgresql/data`) replaces the base bind for the same target
#     and turns create_host_path back ON: a missing source becomes a fresh, empty
#     directory and Postgres initializes an empty database that passes its healthcheck.
#   - Compose merges service `volumes:` by container target (an entry here REPLACES the
#     base entry for that target), but merges `ports:` by APPEND. Never put `ports:`
#     here (Entry 239: an override port stacked on the base binds → EADDRINUSE and a
#     LAN-exposed core-api).
#   - Data binds only. Nothing else belongs in a host override; anything host-specific
#     that is not a secret goes in .env, and secrets go in .env.secrets.
#   - Never delete or rewrite a live override without a backup copy; an empty override
#     file can fail the render — delete the file instead of emptying it.
#   - scripts/test-compose-data-binds.sh renders base + this template in CI and fails if
#     it drifts to short syntax, appends instead of replacing, or touches anything else.
#
# Homeserver transition (2026-11): the live host override still carries the ADR-0004
# SHORT-syntax entries for these two targets. Keep them until the host runs a compose
# file from main at or after item 4.3 (item 5.5) — the host's older compose still
# declares named volumes, and the override is what keeps the live data attached. Then
# remove the postgres entry immediately before the Postgres recreate (item 8.2), the
# redis entry immediately before the Redis recreate (item 8.3), and delete the file
# once it holds no entry. The base binds render the same live paths by default.
services:
  postgres:
    volumes:
      - type: bind
        source: /CHANGE_ME/open-brain/pgdata
        target: /var/lib/postgresql/data
        bind:
          create_host_path: false
  redis:
    volumes:
      - type: bind
        source: /CHANGE_ME/open-brain/redis-data
        target: /data
        bind:
          create_host_path: false
